design.ownerExperience:
There is nothing to set up and no one-time owner step. It arrives with a normal console update: no passkey, no Tailscale change, no download.

- The owner types "What can you do?" in the chat, on the phone too. Sparkie makes one lookup. It reads local files only, so the answer is the same with Spark 3 and 4 off. The reply is a short grouped list:
  - what it can look at, change and remember, each with two or three sentences to say;
  - the workflows the owner saved, by name;
  - the model setups that have worked on these Sparks;
  - the ways in: this chat, /mcp for agents, /v1 for apps, POST /actions for scripts;
  - what it never does: SSH, Tailscale, firewall, users and access, its own model, Spark 2 as a model host, deleting.
- "Show me everything you can change" or "What have I taught you so far?" gives that one part in full: every saved workflow with its steps and last run, how many lines it remembers, and the setups proven here.
- "Which connectors and apps are set up?" gets an honest answer today: none, because those are not abilities of this build. It then names what is connected now: the owner's agents (and whether each may change things) and the four ways in. When connectors and hosted apps are built, they show up here by themselves.
- Asking for something it can't do ("host a website at a URL") gets "I can't do that yet" and the nearest thing it can do, not made-up steps.
- The owner's agents get the same answer: tools/call what_can_you_do over /mcp, or POST /console/api/actions/what_can_you_do with {} or {"about":"change"}. The POST works while the brain is down. An agent that connects also reads a two-sentence version in the MCP instructions.
- Nothing is pushed: no notification, no new page, no button.
